  "summary": "Back-up lamp (reverse light) switch on the transmission and the oil pressure gauge line (oil pressure hose/pipe) from the engine to the dash, all models. The back-up switch bolts to the transmission and is worked by a rod clipped to the reverse lever; its wiring is clipped and riveted near the speedo cable clip. The oil pressure hose screws onto a fitting in the engine block, runs taped to the tach cable, and goes through the firewall grommet (UPC 12) to the instrument panel.",
